@prefix ds:      <https://ds42.org/ns/registry#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:     <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix dcat:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#> .
@prefix dspace:  <https://w3id.org/dspace/2025/1/> .
@prefix did:     <https://www.w3.org/ns/did#> .
@prefix foaf:    <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/> .
@prefix org:     <http://www.w3.org/ns/org#> .
@prefix gx:      <https://w3id.org/gaia-x/2404#> .
@prefix ids:     <https://w3id.org/idsa/core/> .

#
# The ds42 participant registry vocabulary.
#
# Describes the four ADR-0009 membership roles (connector, authority,
# federation-list, service) and the properties a registry entry
# (entries/<role>/<slug>.jsonld in ds-labs-org/ds42-registry) carries. See
# dataspace's docs/adr/0010-*.md for why the registry uses JSON-LD/OWL/
# SHACL rather than plain YAML/JSON Schema — this hub's own domain (DSP,
# DCAT, ODRL) is RDF-based, so the registry describing itself in RDF is
# consistency, not decoration.
#
# `https://ds42.org/ns/registry#` is a namespace this hub controls but
# does not yet serve as a dereferenceable document — same "worked
# example, not yet standing infrastructure" status as everything else
# this study hasn't wired up a live endpoint for. Validation
# (schema/shapes.ttl) does not require it to resolve.
#
# --- Grounding in existing dataspace/identity vocabularies ---------------
#
# This vocabulary deliberately does not stand alone. Every class/property
# below is linked, where a genuine correspondence exists, to a real term
# from an established vocabulary this hub's own domain already depends
# on — verified against each vocabulary's actual current definition
# rather than assumed, so a link below is either `rdfs:subPropertyOf`/
# `rdfs:subClassOf` (a confident, checked equivalence) or `rdfs:seeAlso`
# (a genuine relation, stated without asserting the two terms mean
# exactly the same thing — used where the external vocabulary's own
# scope is broader/narrower/differently-shaped than this registry's, or
# its current definition wasn't independently confirmed against a primary
# source). No `owl:imports` of any of these: none is a dependency this
# repository's own tooling needs to fetch, and asserting a hard import on
# a vocabulary whose long-term URL stability wasn't verified here would
# be the same kind of overclaiming this repo's `CLAUDE.md` warns against
# elsewhere (`authority/`'s placeholders, ADR-0009's deferred items).
#
# - **DCAT** (`dcat:`, W3C Data Catalog Vocabulary,
#   <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#>) — the vocabulary the Dataspace Protocol
#   itself reuses for catalogs and service endpoints (see dspace: below);
#   `ds:endpoint` is a `dcat:endpointURL` by another name for exactly that
#   reason.
# - **The Dataspace Protocol's own vocabulary** (`dspace:`,
#   <https://w3id.org/dspace/2025/1/>, confirmed from its published
#   `context.jsonld`) — the protocol this hub exists to experiment with.
#   DSP's own context defines `dspace:participantId` (a dataspace
#   participant's identifier) and `dspace:CatalogService` (a
#   catalog-serving component), both linked below, and itself reuses
#   `dcat:` and `did:` (see below) rather than minting everything fresh —
#   this vocabulary follows the same reuse discipline.
# - **International Data Spaces (IDS) Information Model** (`ids:`,
#   <https://w3id.org/idsa/core/>) — DSP's direct ancestor (IDSA
#   contributed the initial Dataspace Protocol specification). IDS defines
#   its own `ids:Participant` class — confirmed from the published
#   ontology, not assumed — as a *certified, legally-named* entity
#   (`legalName`, `jurisdiction`, `legalForm`, `participantCertification`).
#   This is the actual, closest naming echo to worry about, and exactly
#   why `ds:ParticipantEntry` is not named bare `Participant`: it does not
#   carry, require, or imply IDS-style certification or legal-entity
#   attributes, so it is linked via `rdfs:seeAlso` only, with this
#   disambiguation stated rather than left implicit.
# - **W3C DID Core** (`did:`, <https://www.w3.org/ns/did#>) —
#   `did:serviceEndpoint` (DID Core §5.6) is the term DSP's own context
#   reuses for endpoint URLs associated with a subject's identity; ds42's
#   `ds:onboardingUrl` — an authority's identity/credential-issuance
#   endpoint — is the same shape of thing.
# - **Gaia-X** (`gx:`, namespace pattern
#   <https://w3id.org/gaia-x/{version}#>, `2404` = the 24.04 Trust
#   Framework release) — the closest existing prior art for exactly this
#   registry's purpose: participant self-descriptions as JSON-LD,
#   validated by SHACL shapes (the same combination this registry
#   independently arrived at), built on DCAT for resources and the W3C
#   Organization Ontology for participants. Gaia-X's own self-description
#   credentials type a participant as `gx:LegalParticipant`. ds42's
#   entries are related in kind — a participant declaring itself into a
#   dataspace — but are a much lighter-weight role declaration, not a
#   full legal-entity self-description (no legal name, registration
#   number, or registered address), so classes below are linked via
#   `rdfs:seeAlso` rather than asserted equivalent to Gaia-X's.
# - **W3C Organization Ontology** (`org:`,
#   <http://www.w3.org/ns/org#>) and **FOAF** (`foaf:`,
#   <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/>) — what Gaia-X itself grounds
#   participant modelling in; linked here for the same reason, softly
#   (`rdfs:seeAlso`), since a ds42 entry names a participant rather than
#   modelling it as a full `org:Organization`/`foaf:Agent` resource.
#
<https://ds42.org/ns/registry>
  a owl:Ontology ;
  rdfs:label "ds42 participant registry vocabulary" ;
  rdfs:comment "Classes and properties for ds42.org's participant registry entries (entries/<role>/<slug>.jsonld in ds-labs-org/ds42-registry)." ;
  dcterms:isPartOf <https://ds42.org> ;
  dcterms:relation dcat: , dspace: , did: , foaf: , org: , gx: , ids: .

# --- Classes -----------------------------------------------------------

ds:ParticipantEntry
  a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Participant entry" ;
  rdfs:comment "A ds42 member's declaration of one role it holds. Abstract: real entries are typed as exactly one of the four concrete subclasses below, per ADR-0009's four ways to participate. Deliberately named ParticipantEntry, not bare Participant: IDS's ids:Participant and Gaia-X's gx:LegalParticipant both denote a certified/legally-named entity (legalName, jurisdiction, participantCertification and similar) — a ds42 entry is a much lighter-weight role declaration and carries none of that, so it is related to both via rdfs:seeAlso only, never asserted equivalent." ;
  rdfs:seeAlso ids:Participant , gx:LegalParticipant , org:Organization , foaf:Agent .

ds:Connector
  a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf ds:ParticipantEntry ;
  rdfs:label "Connector" ;
  rdfs:comment "A DSP participant: publishes a catalog, negotiates contracts, transfers data. The baseline ds42 role." ;
  rdfs:seeAlso dcat:DataService .

ds:Authority
  a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf ds:ParticipantEntry ;
  rdfs:label "Authority" ;
  rdfs:comment "A trust anchor: issues participant credentials and defines an onboarding scheme. ds42 expects several, run by different members; the hub operates none itself. Its trust model is typically DID-based (see ds:trustModel) and its issuance role corresponds to an 'issuer' in the W3C Verifiable Credentials Data Model." .

ds:FederationList
  a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf ds:ParticipantEntry ;
  rdfs:label "Federation list" ;
  rdfs:comment "A catalog broker: harvests other participants' catalogs and re-serves them for discovery. Speaking only part of DSP is a legitimate membership shape, not a deficiency. Broader than DSP's own dspace:CatalogService (a catalog-serving component type within one participant's self-description) — a ds42 federation list is a distinct, separately-registered participant that aggregates *other* participants' catalogs, closer to the eclipse-edc federated-catalog / ds-catalog-broker-rs pattern this study has already vendored/tracked." ;
  rdfs:seeAlso dspace:CatalogService .

ds:Service
  a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf ds:ParticipantEntry ;
  rdfs:label "Service" ;
  rdfs:comment "Anything else the network is more useful for having: vocabulary/shape-validation endpoints, policy-decision services, identity resolution hosting, a conformance-suite runner, monitoring, a looking glass." .

# --- Properties common to every entry -----------------------------------

ds:slug
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain ds:ParticipantEntry ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "slug" ;
  rdfs:comment "Short, URL-safe identifier for this participant (pattern ^[a-z0-9-]+$), unique within its role. Must match the entry's own file name and the last segment of its @id. Registry-local and human-chosen, not necessarily the same value/format as a dspace:participantId used in a live DSP exchange — the same *kind* of identifier, not asserted to be interchangeable with it." ;
  rdfs:seeAlso dspace:participantId .

ds:contact
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain ds:ParticipantEntry ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "contact" ;
  rdfs:comment "A GitHub handle or URL a stranger can use to reach this participant." ;
  rdfs:seeAlso foaf:Agent .

ds:dateRegistered
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:created ;
  rdfs:domain ds:ParticipantEntry ;
  rdfs:range xsd:date ;
  rdfs:label "date registered" ;
  rdfs:comment "YYYY-MM-DD this entry was first submitted." .

ds:description
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:description ;
  rdfs:domain ds:ParticipantEntry ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "description" ;
  rdfs:comment "Optional free-text: what this participant runs or offers." .

ds:registeredBy
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain ds:ParticipantEntry ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "registered by" ;
  rdfs:comment "Informational only, set automatically by the Get started wizard: the GitHub login that opened the registering PR. Never trusted by CI for authorization — see schema/shapes.ttl and dataspace's ADR-0010 for the actual (git-blame-based) authorship check." .

# --- Authority-specific properties ---------------------------------------

ds:trustModel
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain ds:Authority ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "trust model" ;
  rdfs:comment "The trust model this authority operates under (DID/SSI, eIDAS2/PKI, from-scratch, etc.)." .

ds:claimsIssued
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain ds:Authority ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "claims issued" ;
  rdfs:comment "What claims/credentials this authority issues, and to whom." ;
  rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.w3.org/2018/credentials#VerifiableCredential> .

ds:onboardingUrl
  a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:subPropertyOf did:serviceEndpoint ;
  rdfs:domain ds:Authority ;
  rdfs:label "onboarding URL" ;
  rdfs:comment "Where a participant goes to onboard and request a credential from this authority. Same shape of term as did:serviceEndpoint (DID Core §5.6) — a service endpoint associated with this authority's identity — which is exactly what the Dataspace Protocol's own context reuses did:serviceEndpoint for." .

# --- Connector / federation-list / service property ----------------------

ds:endpoint
  a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:subPropertyOf dcat:endpointURL ;
  rdfs:domain [ a owl:Class ; owl:unionOf (ds:Connector ds:FederationList ds:Service) ] ;
  rdfs:label "endpoint" ;
  rdfs:comment "A URL confirming this participant is actually running something (CI's reachability probe — liveness only, not a Dataspace Protocol conformance check; see dataspace's ADR-0010). The same term DSP's own context uses (dcat:endpointURL) for a service's reachable address, reused here rather than re-derived." .

# --- Cardinality restrictions (descriptive; schema/shapes.ttl is what CI
#     actually enforces — see that file's header for why the split) -------

ds:Authority rdfs:subClassOf
  [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty ds:trustModel ;   owl:minCardinality 1 ] ,
  [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty ds:claimsIssued ; owl:minCardinality 1 ] ,
  [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty ds:onboardingUrl ; owl:minCardinality 1 ] .

ds:Connector rdfs:subClassOf
  [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty ds:endpoint ; owl:minCardinality 1 ] .

ds:FederationList rdfs:subClassOf
  [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty ds:endpoint ; owl:minCardinality 1 ] .

ds:Service rdfs:subClassOf
  [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty ds:endpoint ; owl:minCardinality 1 ] .
